# =============================================================================
# mmWave Presence Lighting Node — .gitignore
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Written 2026-09-07 when this project first went into version control.
# =============================================================================

# ---- CREDENTIALS -----------------------------------------------------------
# The firmware here resolves every credential through !secret, and the file
# those resolve against lives in the Home Assistant config, NOT in this repo.
# This block exists so a copy can never wander in.
#
# HISTORY, because it nearly happened: draft/esphome/mmwave-bench.yaml carried
# the Wi-Fi SSID and PSK, the API encryption key and the OTA password in
# plaintext right up until this repo was created. A PSK committed once is
# effectively permanent — it survives in history, in every clone and in every
# fork, and later edits do not remove it. Private repos are not a boundary for
# that: visibility gets flipped, tokens leak, forks outlive intentions.
secrets.yaml
secrets.yml
*.secret
*.key
!*.kicad_sym

# ---- KiCad generated / local ----------------------------------------------
# Auto-backups are regenerated on every save and were 3.8 MB of zip churn.
*-backups/
# Per-user local project state — window layout, last-opened sheet. Not design.
*.kicad_prl
# Editor and tool leftovers
*~
*.bak
*.bck
*.kicad_pcb-bak
*.kicad_sch-bak
fp-info-cache
\#auto_saved_files#

# ---- Vendor archives -------------------------------------------------------
# REVISED 2026-09-08. The rule here used to be "commit the .zip, ignore the
# extraction" — it cost ~15 MB less, and it was wrong for two of the three.
#
# The board names 3D models by path, and two of those paths point INSIDE these
# extractions:
#   U2 alt 1  ${KIPRJMOD}/3d/ld2410c-mmwave-sensor-1.snapshot.2/LD2410C mmWave Sensor.step
#   U2 alt 2  ${KIPRJMOD}/3d/HLK-LD2410C-3D图/HLK-LD2410C.step
# Ignoring those directories did not save 15 MB, it shipped a board file with
# two references nothing in a fresh clone could resolve. Both are now committed.
# They are hidden alternates, so the failure was silent — the 3D view looked
# right and only the alternate was gone. That is why this is spelled out.
#
# Adafruit VEML7700/ stays ignored: the board has no footprint for that part
# (it lives off-board on a QT cable, §3.1), so nothing references the
# extraction, and the .zip beside it is the vendor deliverable.
Adafruit VEML7700/

# ---- Python ----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# ---- OS --------------------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
